{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetN82yK15ckATFH14TvD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough information to complete the analysis.\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- Error responses use sealed `ApiException` hierarchy: `ResourceNotFoundException` (404), `ConflictException` (409), `ValidationException` (400)\n- All errors are wrapped in consistent `ApiError` envelope with `code`, `message`, `fields` via `GlobalExceptionHandler`\n- Controllers throw exceptions rather than building error responses\n- Controllers directly call repositories (no service layer)\n- Tests use MockMvc with `jsonPath` assertions on response bodies\n- Tests assert both status and error `code` for failures (see OrderControllerTest:62, ShipmentControllerTest:55)\n- In-memory repositories are used for testing without external infrastructure\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — Must add `status: OrderStatus` field; Order is a data class, changing it requires versioning\n2. `OrderRepository.kt` — No changes needed; existing methods sufficient\n3. `OrderController.kt` — Must add `cancel` endpoint\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Must add `findByOrderId` method to locate shipments for cancellation\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must validate cancelled orders prevent new shipments\n6. `ApiError.kt` — Must add `ORDER_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS` error codes\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for cancel endpoint cases\n8. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add test for shipment creation validation against cancelled orders\n\n**Risks:**\n- Changing `Order` data class breaks its signature; must update controller's response in all tests\n- Shipment cancellation during order cancellation must be atomic in the in-memory store (ConcurrentHashMap)\n- The shipment creation currently doesn't validate the order exists; adding that check could break existing behavior if tests rely on orphan shipments\n\n**Open questions:** None. The requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `status: OrderStatus` enum field with ACTIVE and CANCELLED states. Create new `OrderStatus` enum.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: Add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 with `ORDER_NOT_FOUND` if order doesn't exist\n   - Throws `ConflictException` with `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` if any shipment is CONFIRMED (all-or-nothing: no state changes)\n   - Returns the cancelled order if already cancelled (idempotent)\n   - Transitions order to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, returns the order with 200 status\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt**: Add method to find all shipments for an order to support cancellation; modify `save` to handle order status updates.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt**: In the `create` endpoint, validate that the order exists and is not CANCELLED before creating a shipment.\n\n6. **ApiError.kt**: Add two new error codes:\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` for 409 when cancellation is blocked by confirmed shipment\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` for 409 when attempting to create shipment for cancelled order\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order succeeds and transitions it to CANCELLED\n   - Cancelling an already CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment fails with 409 and no state changes\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n   - GET /orders/{orderId} after cancel shows CANCELLED status\n   - CREATED shipments are cancelled when order is cancelled\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test for:\n   - Creating a shipment for a CANCELLED order fails with 409 and code `ORDER_CANCELLED`\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Adding a service layer: The existing architecture has no service layer. Adding one would be refactoring unrelated to the ticket scope.\n- Adding an `Order.status` field that is nullable/Optional: The ticket requires a clear ACTIVE or CANCELLED state. Nullable would introduce ambiguity about what null means.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Repository State | Response | HTTP | Code |\n|------|-------|------------------|----------|------|------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | orderId=O-1, status=ACTIVE | Order updates to CANCELLED; matching CREATED shipments become CANCELLED | Order (status=CANCELLED) | 200 | - |\n| Cancel CANCELLED order | orderId=O-1, status=CANCELLED | No change | Order (status=CANCELLED) | 200 | - |\n| Cancel + CONFIRMED shipment | orderId=O-1, CONFIRMED shipment exists | Order stays ACTIVE; shipment unchanged | Error envelope | 409 | ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT |\n| Cancel unknown order | orderId=O-missing | No change | Error envelope | 404 | ORDER_NOT_FOUND |\n| Create shipment on CANCELLED order | orderId=O-1, status=CANCELLED | No change | Error envelope | 409 | ORDER_CANCELLED |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrdered by dependency:\n\n1. **Cancel active order** — Setup: create O-1 with ACTIVE status. Call `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`. Assert 200, order returned with CANCELLED. Call `GET /orders/O-1` and assert CANCELLED. (Covers: creates endpoint, transitions status, persists)\n\n2. **Cancel already-cancelled order** — Setup: O-1 cancelled. Call `POST /orders/O-1/cancel` twice. Assert both 200 with CANCELLED. (Covers: idempotency)\n\n3. **Cancel with confirmed shipment** — Setup: O-1 with shipment S-1 in CONFIRMED. Call `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`. Assert 409 with code `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT`. Call `GET /orders/O-1` and assert ACTIVE. Call `GET /shipments/S-1` and assert CONFIRMED unchanged. (Covers: all-or-nothing, no state change on refusal)\n\n4. **Cancel non-existent order** — Call `POST /orders/does-not-exist/cancel`. Assert 404 with code `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`. (Covers: unknown order handling)\n\n5. **Cancel transitions CREATED shipments** — Setup: O-1 with two shipments S-1 (CREATED) and S-2 (CREATED). Call `POST /orders/O-1/cancel`. Assert order CANCELLED. Call `GET /shipments/S-1` and `GET /shipments/S-2`, assert both CANCELLED. (Covers: cascading cancellation)\n\n6. **Shipment creation blocked for cancelled order** — Setup: O-1 cancelled. Call `POST /shipments` with orderId=O-1. Assert 409 with code `ORDER_CANCELLED`. (Covers: post-cancel constraint)\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes according to the design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":508,"cache_read_input_tokens":22761,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":508},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e13965-c697-42dc-9392-88112fbbf514","uuid":"57327a45-9296-43ac-b90e-6b357b3f69f7","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:48:34.247Z","request_id":"req_011CetN82LbusXcdqbBvUMie"}
