{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetNGQdmG55v3xd1DHCFD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All 19 tests pass (9 order tests, 6 shipment tests, 3 customer tests, 1 application test). \n\n**Command:** `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** BUILD SUCCESS - All tests pass with 0 failures and 0 errors.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ Existing build passes — BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ Existing tests pass — All 19 tests pass (including 4 original order tests, 5 original shipment tests)\n3. ✅ `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels active order, persists, cancels CREATED shipments — Tested: \"cancels an active order and returns the cancelled order\", \"cancelling an order cancels its created shipments\"\n4. ✅ Error responses consistent with rest of API — Uses same ConflictException/ResourceNotFoundException/ErrorCode pattern\n5. ✅ Repeated cancel succeeds; blocked cancel changes nothing; unknown order 404; shipment for cancelled order 409 — All tested in OrderControllerTest and ShipmentControllerTest\n6. ✅ No new Maven dependency — Only Kotlin stdlib and Spring Boot dependencies already present\n7. ✅ No unrelated production file changes — Only order, shipment, and api package files touched\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added `status: OrderStatus` field and `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE/CANCELLED states. Necessary because requirement states \"An order gains a status.\"\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Added:\n   - `status` to Order constructor call\n   - ShipmentRepository injection\n   - `cancel` endpoint implementing all four response cases\n   - All changes necessary for the cancel endpoint\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId` method to find shipments for an order. Necessary to implement cascading cancellation.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added:\n   - OrderRepository injection\n   - Validation in `create` endpoint to reject shipments for cancelled orders\n   - Necessary per requirement: \"Creating a shipment for a cancelled order is rejected with HTTP 409\"\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Added `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` and `ORDER_CANCELLED` error codes. Necessary to report distinct error conditions.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added:\n   - ShipmentRepository injection and clear in reset\n   - Updated existing tests to assert `status` field\n   - 5 new tests covering cancel endpoint cases\n   - Follows testing-and-verification skill: exercises endpoint, re-reads state with separate GET, tests refusal with error code assertion, verifies all-or-nothing rollback\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added:\n   - OrderRepository injection and clear in reset\n   - Updated `createShipment` helper to accept orderId parameter\n   - 1 new test for shipment creation rejection on cancelled order\n   - Follows testing-and-verification skill: asserts response body and error code\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All changes are within scope and necessary.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that transitions orders to CANCELLED status, cascades cancellation to CREATED shipments, rejects if CONFIRMED shipment exists (all-or-nothing), succeeds idempotently on already-cancelled orders, forbids new shipments for cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — Added status: OrderStatus field and OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE/CANCELLED states\n              OrderController.kt — Injected ShipmentRepository, initialized orders with ACTIVE status, added cancel endpoint\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — Added findByOrderId method to locate shipments for cancellation\n              ShipmentController.kt — Injected OrderRepository, validated cancelled order blocks shipment creation\n              ApiError.kt — Added ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — Updated existing tests to assert status field, added 5 tests for cancel endpoint\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — Updated helper and reset, added 1 test for shipment rejection on cancelled order\n\nTests         1. Cancel active order → transitions to CANCELLED, persists, returned in GET\n              2. Cancel already-cancelled → idempotent success\n              3. Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment → 409 with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT, no state change\n              4. Cancel non-existent order → 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n              5. Cancel cascades to CREATED shipments → all CREATED shipments transition to CANCELLED\n              6. Shipment creation blocked for cancelled order → 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test from sample-service/\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS — 19 tests pass (9 order, 6 shipment, 3 customer, 1 application)\n\nNot done      Nothing — all acceptance criteria met, all tests passing, no scope violations\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3329,"cache_read_input_tokens":36472,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3329},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e13965-c697-42dc-9392-88112fbbf514","uuid":"5944e2a0-6322-4741-be54-3f9f7e1cca0e","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:50:23.918Z","request_id":"req_011CetNGPzKeMAz4wtWhLHSQ"}
